From 6dbd5a079a1f0113dea1861e0f2417f1c70b60c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:24:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 78/78] hw/avr: the event recorder and injected faults on the
 AVR64EA48 Nano

The bench's timeline, faults and exact replay for avr64ea48-cnano
(machine "trace=<chardev>"), as on the PIC32CM boards:

- PORT: each pad's level to the recorder (pp_trace_pad(), 8 pads a
  group), "pX-short" (pads shorted to VDD or GND over every driver).
- USART: bytes each way, "rx-inject" (characters into the receiver as
  it has room). TWI: start, byte, host NACK and stop, "fault-nack".
  SPI: transfers, "fault-miso".
- Interrupts: an observer in target/avr (avr_cpu_observe_irqs()) for a
  source asserting its line, the CPU taking the vector and the RETI that
  ends its level (the CPU keeps the vector each level runs). The stream
  numbers them by vector (PP_TRACE_IRQ_VECTORS).
- avr8x_soc_trace() wires the PORT and the observer, then attaches the
  recorder.

qtest avr64ea48-cnano-test: the faults and rx-inject.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
